#X text 860 732 1) Train AND \, OR \, NAND: each settles within a few epochs. Then XOR: the border never settles and the buzzing never stops., f 56;
#X text 860 783 2) Learning rate high = big jumps (fast \, jumpy). Low = small careful steps., f 56;
#X text 860 819 3) Use "one step" and predict where the border moves before you click., f 56;
#X text 860 855 4) MUSIC: x1 \, x2 could be features of a sound (loud? bright?) and the answer could pick a sample: a perceptron is a tiny classifier you can train by example., f 56;
